WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.825
Not all islands are alike.

00:00:01.825 --> 00:00:05.172
Geographers classify them first by the crust they stand on,

00:00:05.172 --> 00:00:07.838
and the process that raised them above the sea.

00:00:08.938 --> 00:00:12.377
Continental islands sit on thick, light continental crust.

00:00:12.377 --> 00:00:15.933
Some, like Britain, are simply parts of a continental shelf,

00:00:15.933 --> 00:00:18.779
joined to the mainland whenever sea level falls.

00:00:18.779 --> 00:00:24.055
Others are fragments of continent that broke away, like Socotra and the Falkland Islands.

00:00:25.155 --> 00:00:26.896
Oceanic islands are different.

00:00:26.896 --> 00:00:30.031
They are volcanoes built up from the deep ocean floor,

00:00:30.031 --> 00:00:32.759
and they have never been joined to a continent.

00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:35.778
Tristan da Cunha and Pitcairn are hotspot volcanoes.

00:00:35.778 --> 00:00:38.216
Surtsey grew on a rift in Iceland's shelf.

00:00:38.216 --> 00:00:42.279
When such a volcano sinks, a coral reef can keep growing on top of it,

00:00:42.279 --> 00:00:44.079
forming an atoll like Funafuti.

00:00:44.079 --> 00:00:49.013
And if an atoll is later pushed up, it becomes a raised atoll, like Henderson Island.

00:00:50.113 --> 00:00:55.008
This is that building process today: lava fountaining at Kīlauea, on Hawaii,

00:00:55.008 --> 00:00:57.520
the youngest island of a hotspot chain.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:03.504
The type predicts a great deal: the rocks, the soils, the relief, the island's age,

00:01:03.504 --> 00:01:07.270
and even what kinds of animals and plants could have reached it.

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:09.117
Two cautions.

00:01:09.117 --> 00:01:13.770
Many islands are composites: Socotra's limestone plateaux sit on ancient granite.

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:15.666
And sea level changes everything.

00:01:15.666 --> 00:01:19.631
At the peak of the last ice age, about twenty-one thousand years ago,

00:01:19.631 --> 00:01:23.193
the sea stood around one hundred and twenty-five metres lower.

00:01:23.193 --> 00:01:27.387
Shelf islands joined their continents, and atolls became limestone hills.
